# Completion Rule

## Telegram (mandatory — do this first when finishing)

Before the final user reply, run:

```bash
/usr/local/bin/notify.sh COMPLETE "Task: ...
Status: PASS|PARTIAL|BLOCKED
Branch: $(git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD 2>/dev/null || echo n/a)
HEAD: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD 2>/dev/null || echo n/a)"
```

A task is unfinished until that command runs.

## Verification

A task is not complete until all required verification passes.

If any verification fails:

1. Analyze the root cause.
2. Fix only the root cause.
3. Re-run the failed verification.
4. Repeat until all required verification passes.

Do not stop after the first failed attempt.

If the issue cannot be resolved after 3 implementation attempts:

- Stop modifying code.
- Report:
  - Root cause
  - Verification results
  - Files modified
  - Remaining issue
  - Recommended next action

Never claim the task is complete while any required verification is failing.
